questions.explanation:
In [Co(<i>ox</i>)_{2}(OH)_{2}]^{$-$}

$Co^{+5}$ = [Ar] $3d^{4}$ (4 unpaired electrons)

OX and OH are weak field ligands.

In [Ti($NH_{3}$)_{6}]^{3+}

$Ti^{+3}$ = [Ar] $3d^{1}$ (one unpaired electron)

In [V(gly)_{2}(OH)_{2}($NH_{3}$)_{2}]^{+}

$V^{+5}$ = [Ar] $4r^{0} 3d^{0}$ (no unpaired electron)

In [Fe(<i>en</i>)(<i>bpy</i>)($NH_{3}$)_{2}]^{2+}

$Fe^{+2}$ = [Ar] $3d^{6}$ (4 unpaired electrons)

But due to presence of strong field ligand like $NH_{3}$, bpy and en thus $Fe^{+2}$ contains no unpaired electron.

$\therefore$ Complex [Co(<i>ox</i>)_{2}(OH)_{2}]^{$-$} has maximum number of unpaired electrons, thus show maximum paramagnetism.
